ng an indicator. After revisiting Train 3 and comparing the maximum counts with each block, the output equals 1, and the background is 0. With more analysis, I discovered that the blocks with the *maximum* number of foreground/marker pixels are assigned 1, and all other blocks are the background color. I'm excited to test this on the test input now!\n\n\n**Verifying Count Patterns**\n\nI'm now counting and checking the number of \"6\"s in each block of a new input. Block by block, I'm noting the counts and comparing them to previously identified trends. I'm verifying the block counts match previous blocks, and the analysis is proving consistent, bolstering my confidence in the current theory. I will be looking closely at any discrepancies to see if I am missing a crucial piece of information.\n\n\n",
